<p><u><a href="https://researchdirectory.uc.edu/p/chemeray" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Anthony Chemero</a></u>, currently professor of philosophy at the <u><a href="https://www.artsci.uc.edu/humanities/philosophy.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Cincinnati</a></u>, will be moving to <u><a href="https://as.vanderbilt.edu/philosophy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vanderbilt University</a></u>.<span id="more-57174"></span></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-57175 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/chemero-anthony.jpeg" alt="" width="207" height="263" /></p>
<p>Professor Chemero works in philosophy of mind, philosophy of science, and phenomenology. He is the author of <em><u><a href="https://cup.columbia.edu/book/intertwined-creatures/9780231223195/">Intertwined Creatures</a></u></em> among other writings, which you can learn more about <a href="https://philpeople.org/profiles/anthony-chemero" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a> and <u><a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=-RAPSx4AAAAJ&amp;hl=en">here</a></u>.</p>
<p>He will be taking up his new position as professor of philosophy at Vanderbilt University this fall.</p>
